{% tool-context
   title="Architecture Decision Workbench"
   question="What is an architecture decision?"
   definition="An architecture decision is a consequential technical choice with explicit context, viable alternatives, and accepted downsides. A useful decision record explains why the choice is defensible and what evidence could overturn it."
   inputs="Model traffic, latency, consistency, data shape, geography, and operating capacity. Compare candidates before selecting the path your team is prepared to own."
   outcome="Leave with a ranked alternative, a visible serving path, explicit contradictions, required mitigations, and a shareable architecture decision record."
   experiment="Choose a candidate, then inject a traffic spike, region loss, hot partition, or replication lag. Increase severity until the recommendation changes or an accepted downside becomes a user-visible failure." /%}

